=== Petition ===
On 30 December 2020 the NDC filed a petition at the Supreme Court challenging the results.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ghana opposition seeks to overturn Akufo-Addo's election win |url=https://www.dw.com/en/ghana-opposition-seeks-to-overturn-akufo-addos-election-win/a-56096712|access-date=2020-12-31|website=Deutsche Welle|language=en-GB}}</ref> On 4 March 2021 the Supreme Court unanimously dismissed the petition, stated that it lacked merit.<ref>{{Cite news|title=Supreme Court fixes March 4 as judgement day for 2020 election petition|url=https://www.graphic.com.gh/news/politics/supreme-court-fixes-march-4-as-judgement-day-for-2020-election-petition.html|location=Accra, Ghana|access-date=2021-05-21|newspaper=[[Daily Graphic (Ghana)|Daily Graphic]]|language=en-gb}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news|title=Why the Supreme Court dismissed Mahama's 2020 presidential election petition (FULL JUDGMENT)|url=https://www.graphic.com.gh/news/politics/why-the-supreme-court-dismissed-mahama-s-2020-presidential-election-petition-full-judgment.html|location=Accra, Ghana|first=Enoch Darfah|last=Frimpong|date=5 March 2021|access-date=2021-11-11|newspaper=[[Daily Graphic (Ghana)|Daily Graphic]]|language=en-gb}}</ref>

